WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.083
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:18.862
Unit twelve: Writing Task 1: Comparing Data and Overview. Today you will compare figures in bar charts, pie charts and tables, and write a clear overview.

4
00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:21.768
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:26.140
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:27.915
Compare.

7
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:31.555
Compare means to show how things are alike or different.

8
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.732
Compare the two groups.

9
00:00:34.317 --> 00:00:36.830
Your turn. Say: Compare.

10
00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:40.656
Compare.

11
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:42.290
Whereas.

12
00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:45.979
Whereas means used to contrast two facts.

13
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:49.129
Men spent more, whereas women saved.

14
00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:52.021
Your turn. Say: Whereas.

15
00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:55.926
Whereas.

16
00:00:56.683 --> 00:00:57.661
Proportion.

17
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.638
Proportion means a part of a whole.

18
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.739
A large proportion walked.

19
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.513
Your turn. Say: Proportion.

20
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.391
Proportion.

21
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.163
Highest.

22
00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.184
Highest means the greatest in number.

23
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:17.527
Tea had the highest figure.

24
00:01:18.117 --> 00:01:20.583
Your turn. Say: Highest.

25
00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:24.307
Highest.

26
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:25.981
Lowest.

27
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:29.296
Lowest means the smallest in number.

28
00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:31.662
Coffee had the lowest figure.

29
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.682
Your turn. Say: Lowest.

30
00:01:37.533 --> 00:01:38.383
Lowest.

31
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.116
Overview.

32
00:01:41.117 --> 00:01:43.813
Overview means a summary of the main features.

33
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.731
Write an overview.

34
00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:48.772
Your turn. Say: Overview.

35
00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:52.611
Overview.

36
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.514
Approximately.

37
00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:58.259
Approximately means about, not exactly.

38
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.815
Approximately 40 percent.

39
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:04.905
Your turn. Say: Approximately.

40
00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:08.965
Approximately.

41
00:02:09.717 --> 00:02:10.497
Double.

42
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:13.669
Double means to become twice as much.

43
00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:15.517
The number doubled.

44
00:02:16.117 --> 00:02:18.653
Your turn. Say: Double.

45
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.315
Double.

46
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.693
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.422
Visal, what is an overview?

48
00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:41.087
An overview is two or three sentences that summarise the main features without too many numbers. Without an overview you cannot score highly for Task Achievement.

49
00:02:42.183 --> 00:02:43.846
How do I compare data?

50
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:55.474
Use comparative and superlative forms and linking words. For example, tea was the most popular drink, whereas juice was the least popular.

51
00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:58.026
How do I use numbers?

52
00:02:59.117 --> 00:03:07.539
Select key figures, group similar data and use approximately for rounded numbers. Do not describe every single number.

53
00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.583
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.992
Grammar focus: Strategy: select, group, compare.

55
00:03:16.292 --> 00:03:17.467
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:22.191
Tea was the most popular drink, whereas juice was the least popular.

57
00:03:23.083 --> 00:03:27.115
Overall, the figures show that hot drinks were preferred to cold drinks.

58
00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:36.942
Write an overview that gives the main features, and then support it with key figures. Use comparatives, superlatives and linking words such as whereas and while.

59
00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:41.195
Be careful! Don't say: I describe every single number.

60
00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:46.004
Say: I select and group key figures.

61
00:03:46.304 --> 00:03:47.920
Select key figures.

62
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:51.351
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:53.760
A Bar Chart on Drinks.

64
00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.824
The bar chart compares the drinks chosen by 200 students.

65
00:03:58.833 --> 00:04:03.190
Approximately 80 students chose tea, which was the highest figure.

66
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.626
Coffee was chosen by about 60, whereas juice had the lowest figure of 20.

67
00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:13.177
Overall, hot drinks were much more popular than cold drinks.

68
00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:18.001
The number of tea drinkers was four times the number of juice drinkers.

69
00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:23.067
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:23.917 --> 00:04:25.278
An overview blank.

71
00:04:25.578 --> 00:04:31.205
A, summarises main features. B, lists every number. C, gives opinions.

72
00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:37.660
The answer is A: summarises main features.

73
00:04:38.817 --> 00:04:40.503
'Whereas' is used to blank.

74
00:04:40.803 --> 00:04:44.595
A, give a reason. B, contrast. C, add.

75
00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.075
The answer is B: contrast.

76
00:04:51.217 --> 00:04:53.042
Approximately means blank.

77
00:04:53.342 --> 00:04:57.112
A, exactly. B, never. C, about.

78
00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.341
The answer is C: about.

79
00:05:03.483 --> 00:05:05.471
Which drink had the highest figure?

80
00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:09.030
A, tea. B, coffee. C, juice.

81
00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:14.171
The answer is A: tea.

82
00:05:15.317 --> 00:05:18.431
Without an overview, the writer loses marks for blank.

83
00:05:18.731 --> 00:05:22.941
A, handwriting. B, Task Achievement. C, spelling only.

84
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.987
The answer is B: Task Achievement.

85
00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.468
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:34.317 --> 00:05:36.653
Why is an overview important in Task 1?

87
00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.811
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:47.111 --> 00:06:04.220
An overview summarises the main features of the data, so the reader understands the big picture. It shows that I can select the most important information, and it improves my score for Task Achievement. I always write it after the introduction.

89
00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.241
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:12.484
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: select, group, compare.

91
00:06:12.784 --> 00:06:17.654
Today's value is analytical thinking. Look for the pattern underneath the surface.

92
00:06:17.954 --> 00:06:20.664
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:20.964 --> 00:06:23.617
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

